course: dictionary
lesson: 5296
title: The jury
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A jury is a group of ordinary people who help decide a court case. «A jury is twelve ordinary adults picked at random who listen to a criminal trial and decide whether the person is guilty or not guilty.» The clues are ordinary adults, listen and decide. A jury listens, then makes a decision.
explain: Jury has a second meaning too. At school, a jury can be judges who pick the best poem or science project. Read the words around it to know which meaning fits. A court case means the court sense; a competition means the school sense.
explain: Two words in court are easy to mix up. «The verdict is the jury's decision, guilty or not guilty; the sentence is the punishment the judge gives.» The jury gives the verdict, and the judge gives the sentence. Phrases like «the jury is out» mean people have not decided yet.
fact: A jury is a group of people who judge something together.
fact: In a court, a jury is usually twelve ordinary adults who decide if someone is guilty or not guilty.
fact: «Verdict» means the decision of the jury.
fact: «Sentence» means the punishment the judge gives after a guilty verdict.
fact: «The jury is out» means people have not decided yet.
exercise: In a court case, who decides whether someone is guilty or not guilty? | The judge | The lawyer | The police officer | *The jury
exercise: Ms Patel says, «The jury is out on the best science project.» What does this mean? | The science project is out of the school | *The judges have not decided yet | Everyone agrees on the best project | The project has finished and won
exercise: «The verdict is the jury's decision; the sentence is the punishment the judge gives.» Which word means the punishment? | *Sentence | Jury | Witness | Verdict
test: «After 1215, juries of ordinary people, usually twelve, grew in England.» How many people does a jury usually have? | One hundred | Twenty | Six | *Twelve
test: At school, a jury of judges picks the best poem. In this sentence, what does jury mean? | A court of law | A type of poem | *A group who judge a competition and choose the winner | A group of children
exam: What is the name for a jury's decision, guilty or not guilty? | *Verdict | Trial | Sentence | Witness
